AUDIO: 'that\'s a really effective way to be thinking about this. But a problem we still have is I hear from so many people that they don\'t even know what angles or shots to be grabbing in the first place. The most important foundation here and the thing I\'m so excited about is my'

[04:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'favorite technique of all time. I promise this will be one of the most high value skills you can learn with 360. And you\'ll see as we move through this video how important this foundation is so we can stack these skills together and improve every aspect about what it'

[04:52] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: The creator stands in an outdoor plaza, gesturing, explaining camera placement.
AUDIO: 'is that you\'re creating. When you hit record on a 360 camera, it is always filming in every direction. And so that means for every single shot of video you capture, you\'re actually capturing an'

[05:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'infinite possibility of refframe shots. And because the camera has lenses on both sides, it\'s filming in all directions. And if there\'s a stick in the middle, it simply just disappears.'

[05:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And that\'s what creates the floating camera look. So now whenever you pick up the selfie stick, you get a camera that just follows you around as if you\'re not actually using a selfie stick, which'

[05:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'makes end results that look kind of impossible to capture. Because it films in all directions, it really opens up some really creative possibilities for mounting the camera. You will guaranteed get lots of'

[05:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'questions from people of how did you record that shot? So, as we get into the technique, I also have an accessory deep dive video coming up on the channel where I basically unpack every single accessory that I actually use and find'

